.saivage/stages/cycle-008-implement-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reports/t1-implement-wave-008-restructure.json:6:  "summary": "Implemented Wave 008 Proposal Restructure. ThreeView.vue is now a lifecycle/composition shell that reads injected World, display options, and selected IDs, then delegates mount/refresh/resize/dispose to ThreeViewRuntime. Added concern-split threePresentation selectors/read models for projection planes/axes/labels, planar 2D-on-3D elements, reconstructed 3D elements, guides/selected perpendicular planes/intersections, and hinge lines. Added DTO-only Three.js scene runtime/host/adapters and ThreeObjectRegistry with grouped replacement and CSS2D label cleanup semantics. Deleted frontend/src/services/Element2DRenderer3D.ts and old raw-World renderer usage. Added focused unit tests for selector orchestration, adapter DTO conversion, registry disposal, and CSS2D label cleanup. Wrote architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/implementation-log.md with changed files, deletions, validation logs, blockers, and out-of-scope guards. Focused Vitest passed. Build/typecheck attempts were logged; vue-tsc is blocked by an existing Node 24/vue-tsc issue and whole-project tsc reports many pre-existing unrelated errors, with one in-scope adapter issue fixed before final focused test rerun.",
