architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/scope-check.md:8:- Secret-safety note: this check used source files, baseline/wave artifacts, package scripts, and test filenames only; it did not read `.saivage/saivage.json`, auth profiles, env files, provider configs, OAuth/Drive credentials, or shell history.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/scope-check.md:14:The current tree still matches Wave 008's central premise: `ThreeView.vue` is a large 3D rendering god component, and `Element2DRenderer3D.ts` is a service-shaped raw scene renderer that still reaches directly into `World`, projection planes, realizations, visibility policy, and Three.js object construction. Wave 007 changed the 2D rendering path by adding a selector/read-model boundary, but it intentionally did not touch `ThreeView.vue`, `Element2DRenderer3D.ts`, or 3D scene adapters. That means Wave 008 remains the next central rendering-boundary cleanup after 2D selector extraction.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/scope-check.md:16:No plan edit is needed because the wave's target outcome remains exactly right: make `ThreeView.vue` a lifecycle/composition shell over focused scene adapters/selectors, isolating scene setup, projection-plane meshes, labels, guide/hinge geometry, domain-to-view conversion, and 2D-on-plane / reconstructed-3D object rendering.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/scope-check.md:22:- Vue/store/domain wiring is embedded in the component: it imports Vue lifecycle/watch/inject, Three.js, OrbitControls, CSS2DRenderer/CSS2DObject, domain `World`, `ProjectionPlane`, `AuxiliaryProjectionPlane`, `Plane3DRealization3D`, rendering config, both `viewStore` and `selectionStore`, domain guide predicates, grid utilities, and coordinate utilities in one script block (`frontend/src/components/panels/ThreeView.vue:35-77`).
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/scope-check.md:27:- Fallback grid creation is inline (`frontend/src/components/panels/ThreeView.vue:84-105`) even though grid/read-model style responsibilities now have precedent in Wave 007's canvas selectors.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/scope-check.md:46:- `resolveVisualStyle()` is a local placeholder with a TODO and default blue style rather than consuming explicit selector DTO styles (`frontend/src/services/Element2DRenderer3D.ts:384-402`).
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/scope-check.md:60:The 3D rendering path uses domain realization APIs that should be consumed behind a selector/read-model boundary, not directly throughout a Vue component.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/scope-check.md:62:- Projection-plane 3D realization lookup lives on `World.getProjectionPlane3DRealization()` (`frontend/src/domain/world/World.ts:588`).
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/scope-check.md:63:- Reconstructed 3D collections live on `World.getAllPlanes()`, `World.getAllHingeLines()`, `World.getAll3DPoints()`, `World.getAll3DLines()`, and `World.getAll3DSegments()` (`frontend/src/domain/world/World.ts:884`, `frontend/src/domain/world/World.ts:916`, `frontend/src/domain/world/World.ts:1105`, `frontend/src/domain/world/World.ts:1138`, `frontend/src/domain/world/World.ts:1171`).
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/scope-check.md:64:- Realization lookups live on `World.get3DPlane()`, `World.get3DPointRealization()`, `World.get3DLineRealization()`, `World.get3DSegmentRealization()`, and `World.get3DPlaneRealization()` (`frontend/src/domain/world/World.ts:1187`, `frontend/src/domain/world/World.ts:1221`, `frontend/src/domain/world/World.ts:1240`, `frontend/src/domain/world/World.ts:1259`, `frontend/src/domain/world/World.ts:1278`).
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/scope-check.md:65:- Hinge lines and guide/domain elements also call back into projection-plane realization APIs internally, which reinforces that the selector boundary must be careful not to move domain algorithms into scene adapters (`frontend/src/domain/world/HingeLine.ts:173`, `frontend/src/domain/world/HingeLine.ts:193`, `frontend/src/domain/world/Guide.ts:320-321`).
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/scope-check.md:69:Wave 007 completed a 2D presentation boundary rather than a 3D boundary. The implementation log says it added `frontend/src/application/canvasPresentation/` DTOs/selectors/style/visibility/grid/query/controller, deleted `RenderService.ts` and `PaperService.ts`, and intentionally did not refactor `ThreeView.vue` or 3D scene adapters (`architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/implementation-log.md`).
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/scope-check.md:75:- `CanvasPresentationController` is a thin Vue-facing facade over the selector (`frontend/src/application/canvasPresentation/CanvasPresentationController.ts:5-9`).
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/scope-check.md:77:Wave 008 should share this selector/read-model pattern where appropriate, but **must not reopen Wave 007's 2D implementation scope**. The 3D selector can reuse style/visibility concepts or common small policies, but should not reintroduce `PaperService`, `RenderService`, `Paper.hitTest`, 2D canvas grid generation, or direct canvas rendering changes.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/scope-check.md:92:- A debug e2e spec points at `http://localhost:5180` (`frontend/tests/e2e/debug.spec.ts:3-11`), while the main e2e specs use `http://localhost:5173` or `/` (`frontend/tests/e2e/hhl-intersection.spec.ts:17`, `frontend/tests/e2e/parametric-update.spec.ts:18`); Wave 008 validation should record the live-preview URL/probe explicitly instead of assuming debug-spec coverage of the 3D view.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/scope-check.md:93:- No current unit-test file path in `frontend/tests/` matches `ThreeView` or `Element2DRenderer3D` by filename, so Wave 008 implementation should add focused tests for the new 3D presentation selector DTOs and adapter object creation rather than relying on existing domain/e2e coverage.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/scope-check.md:97:No premise invalidation was found for Wave 008. After Wave 007, rendering centrality now points to the 3D path as the next rendering god-module cleanup before broader app shell extraction.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/scope-check.md:100:2. **Wave 009 — Extract application shell services from `App.vue`**: remains next after rendering boundaries are stable, especially because preview/startup and active-plane coordination interact with both canvases.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/scope-check.md:101:3. **Wave 010 — Resolve backend/frontend project-contract architecture**: still depends on persistence/app-shell stance.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/scope-check.md:110:- `frontend/src/components/panels/ThreeView.vue` lifecycle/composition shell extraction.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/scope-check.md:113:- New 3D presentation selector/read-model DTO modules under an application/presentation boundary.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/scope-check.md:115:- Focused unit tests for selector DTO production and adapter object creation using Three.js objects without mounting the whole Vue component where practical.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/scope-check.md:116:- E2e/live preview checks that exercise the visible 3D canvas and representative 3D rendering behavior.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/scope-check.md:120:- Reopening the Wave 007 2D canvas selector/adapter implementation except to consume/share small style/visibility/read-model policies.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/scope-check.md:122:- Changing persistence, backend contracts, or app-shell project lifecycle.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:5:Round-01 correction: the extraction is implementation-ready only if selected IDs enter the `threePresentation` boundary as plain input and all selected-guide/perpendicular-plane DTO production, domain lookup, and scene-object construction are outside `ThreeView.vue`. The read-model side must remain concern-split across projection planes, planar 2D-on-3D elements, reconstructed 3D elements, guides, and hinge/axis geometry; `ThreePresentationSelector.ts` is only an orchestrator, not a replacement god selector. The scene side must validate grouped object replacement, CSS2D label cleanup/replacement, and removal of repeated `scene.children` clearing patterns from `ThreeView.vue`.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:7:Implement Wave 008 as a direct extraction of the existing 3D rendering behavior into focused 3D presentation and Three.js adapter modules. `ThreeView.vue` becomes a Vue lifecycle/composition shell: it owns refs, watchers, injected `World`, display/selection state, and calls a `ThreeViewController`/scene facade. All low-level Three.js object creation and all domain-to-view conversion move out of the component. `ThreeView.vue` may read UI stores for display options and selected IDs, but selected IDs must cross into the `threePresentation` input and guide/perpendicular-plane DTO production plus scene-object construction must live outside the component.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:9:This proposal preserves the current behavior and visual semantics while deleting large inline helpers from the component. It is intentionally smaller than the restructure option: the 3D selector is introduced, but only for the current scene needs; it does not attempt to generalize a cross-2D/3D presentation package.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:19:- Rendering constants already live in `rendering3D.ts` and should be consumed by extracted modules (`frontend/src/config/rendering3D.ts:16-83`).
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:30:- The new selector/read-model boundary mirrors Wave 007's pattern without touching the 2D canvas path. It is not a single replacement god selector: projection planes, planar 2D-on-3D elements, reconstructed 3D elements, guides, and hinge/axis geometry are separate selector/read-model concerns, even if a thin controller orchestrates them.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:32:## Non-negotiable shell and selector boundaries
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:37:- Scene-object construction for projection planes, planar elements, reconstructed elements, guides, hinges, axes, and CSS2D labels lives only in `frontend/src/rendering/threeView/` adapters/host modules.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:38:- The implementation must split read-model construction by concern: projection planes, planar 2D-on-3D elements, reconstructed 3D elements, guides, and hinge/axis geometry each get a focused selector/read-model module or equivalent focused internal module. A monolithic `ThreePresentationSelector` that absorbs all current `ThreeView.vue` and `Element2DRenderer3D` traversal is explicitly rejected.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:42:### Component shell
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:57:  - Thin orchestrator for concern-specific selectors; it must not become the one large replacement god module.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:58:  - Accepts `World`, display options, and selected IDs as input, then delegates to the focused selectors below.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:72:  - May import/reuse existing 2D visibility policy or domain `resolveVisibility` only inside selector/policy, not adapters.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:103:  - Keep as config. Add only missing constants if needed by DTO/style policy; do not add per-plane compatibility shims.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:109:- Add focused selector tests under `frontend/tests/unit/application/threePresentation/`, e.g.:
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:119:- Add or update a Vue shell test under `frontend/tests/unit/components/` only to verify mount calls controller methods and responds to display/selection/world changes without asserting geometry internals.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:120:- Add or update e2e/live smoke coverage for the 3D canvas if feasible; if existing malformed specs still block global e2e, capture and classify as in Wave 007 validation.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:128:  - `initThreeScene()` scene setup body (`frontend/src/components/panels/ThreeView.vue:138-216`) except shell call delegation.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:139:- Delete `frontend/src/services/Element2DRenderer3D.ts` after its responsibilities are replaced by selector DTOs + `PlanarElementSceneAdapter`.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:143:- Delete obsolete tests that assert `Element2DRenderer3D` raw-World traversal if any are discovered; replace with selector/adapter tests.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:165:   - no `new THREE.*`, `scene.children.filter`, `userData.type` scene clearing, `world.projectionPlanes`, `getAll3D*`, `getAllHingeLines`, `realize2D(world)`, or `realize3D(world)` remain in `ThreeView.vue` except allowed shell/controller wiring,
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:176:9. E2e/Playwright: `npm run test:e2e --workspace=frontend`, or classify known malformed e2e blockers with exact logs if still present.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:184:- `ThreeView.vue` shell-boundary scan proves it no longer imports domain projection/guide/hinge types for geometry derivation, no longer performs selected-element domain lookup, and no longer constructs `THREE.*`/`CSS2DObject` objects; it only passes display options, injected `World`, and selected IDs into the runtime/controller.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:189:- Guide selector receives selected IDs from the presentation input and emits perpendicular-plane DTOs plus intersection-marker DTOs for selected guides; `ThreeView.vue` contains no guide-plane math.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:192:- `ThreeView.vue` shell calls controller refresh on world/display/selection changes and resize/dispose on lifecycle.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:196:- **Risk: selector becomes a second god-module.** Mitigation: make the concern split mandatory: projection planes, planar 2D-on-3D elements, reconstructed 3D elements, guides, and hinge/axis geometry are separate selector modules or focused internal modules with tests per concern.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:199:- **Risk: guide/hinge math accidentally moves from domain to adapters.** Mitigation: selectors may call domain realizations, but adapters consume DTO geometry only.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:200:- **Risk: e2e remains blocked by pre-existing malformed specs/tooling.** Mitigation: still run mandatory commands, capture logs, and add focused/live browser smoke to prove 3D behavior where global e2e cannot run.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:204:This addendum resolves the Wave 008 round-01 review blockers and supersedes any earlier wording that could be read as allowing a single god selector or retaining guide/selection geometry in `ThreeView.vue`.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:208:`ThreeView.vue` may read `viewStore`, `selectionStore`, and the injected `World` only as shell-level inputs. It must pass the current display options and selected entity IDs into the `threePresentation` boundary as an explicit input object, for example `ThreePresentationInput { world, displayOptions, selectedIds }`. The component must not perform direct selected-element domain lookup, guide/perpendicular-plane geometry derivation, projection-plane matrix interpretation, domain-to-view coordinate conversion, or raw Three.js object construction after the wave.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:210:Guide/perpendicular-plane behavior is part of the `threePresentation` read-model boundary: selected guide IDs enter the selector input, `Guide3DSelector` resolves selected guides and emits guide perpendicular-plane and guide intersection marker DTOs, and `GuideSceneAdapter` consumes those DTOs to create/replace scene objects. `ThreeView.vue` must only trigger runtime refreshes and must not contain guide/perpendicular-plane DTO production or scene-object construction.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:220:- `Hinge3DSelector` and an axis/label concern (`Axis3DSelector` or the projection-plane selector's axis submodule) for hinge/reference/auxiliary axis geometry and labels.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:222:A single top-level controller may compose these selectors, but no file may absorb all projection-plane, planar-element, reconstructed-element, guide, hinge, and axis traversal. This direct proposal remains a fallback only if it preserves that split.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:237:- shell-boundary static scan proving `ThreeView.vue` contains no `new THREE.*`, `scene.children`, `Float32BufferAttribute`, `LineBasicMaterial`, `MeshBasicMaterial`, `SphereGeometry`, `TubeGeometry`, `PlaneGeometry`, `ArrowHelper`, `CSS2DObject`, direct projection/guide domain realization calls, `world.projectionPlanes`, `getAll3D*`, `getAllHingeLines`, `realize2D(world)`, or `realize3D(world)` except shell/controller wiring;
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:238:- scene setup extraction check proving scene/camera/WebGLRenderer/CSS2DRenderer/OrbitControls/lights/animation/resize/dispose live in `ThreeSceneHost`/runtime, not `ThreeView.vue`;
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:239:- selector tests for projection-plane meshes/grids/labels, planar 2D-on-3D elements, reconstructed 3D elements, guide perpendicular planes/intersections, hinge lines, axes, and domain-to-view conversion metadata;
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:241:- mandatory root and frontend lint/test/build cadence plus e2e/Playwright or exact classification of pre-existing blockers;
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:242:- live 3D smoke proving `canvas.three-canvas` mounts, scene setup occurs through the runtime, display/selection refreshes produce representative 3D groups, and the preview refresh/probe is recorded.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:5:Round-01 correction: the selected Proposal Restructure path is implementation-ready only if `ThreeView.vue` passes display options, injected `World`, and selected IDs into `ThreeViewRuntime`/`threePresentation`, while guide/perpendicular-plane DTO production, selected-element lookup, domain-to-view conversion, and all Three.js/CSS2D object construction live outside the Vue shell. The `threePresentation` package must be concern-split by projection planes, planar 2D-on-3D elements, reconstructed 3D elements, guides, and hinge/axis geometry; the scene host/registry/adapters must own grouped replacement/disposal and CSS2D label lifecycle with focused validation.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:7:Implement Wave 008 one conceptual layer higher than a mechanical `ThreeView.vue` extraction: introduce an application-owned `threePresentation` read-model boundary parallel to Wave 007's `canvasPresentation`, then make Three.js adapters pure consumers of that model. The component delegates lifecycle to a `ThreeViewRuntime`, while all domain traversal happens in selectors and all Three.js mutation happens in adapters.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:9:This option treats `Element2DRenderer3D.ts` as an architectural smell to delete, not merely move. It also avoids letting `ThreeView.vue` call individual adapters directly; the component talks to one runtime/facade that composes selector + scene host + adapters.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:15:- **Domain/application read side:** concern-split `threePresentation` selectors convert `World` + display state + selected IDs into immutable DTOs. Selected IDs are input to the presentation boundary; guide/perpendicular-plane DTO production happens there, not in `ThreeView.vue`.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:17:- **Vue shell side:** `ThreeView.vue` controls lifecycle and UI options only. It may read `viewStore`/`selectionStore` for UI state, but it must not perform selected-element domain lookup, guide/perpendicular-plane math, or raw Three.js/CSS2D object construction.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:57:- `ThreePresentationSelector.ts` is an orchestrator only. Projection planes, planar 2D-on-3D elements, reconstructed 3D elements, guides, and hinge/axis geometry must remain separate selector/read-model concerns; a single large selector file absorbing all old component/service logic is not acceptable.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:62:### Component shell
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:85:  - Orchestrates subselectors and returns one `ThreePresentationModel`.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:136:  - Use from selectors/policies. Move no behavior unless tests prove a pure helper belongs there.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:147:- `frontend/tests/unit/components/ThreeView.shell.spec.ts` or equivalent shell test.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:169:- Delete raw `world.projectionPlanes`, `world.getAll3D*`, `world.getAllHingeLines`, `realize2D(world)`, and `realize3D(world)` calls from `ThreeView.vue` and scene adapters; keep such calls only inside concern-split `application/threePresentation` selectors.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:173:- Delete infinite-line clipping TODO by making line extent/clipping an explicit selector/policy decision (`frontend/src/services/Element2DRenderer3D.ts:172-178`).
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:174:- Delete any obsolete tests/fixtures that instantiate `Element2DRenderer3D` with a raw `World`; replace with selector and adapter tests.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:201:- `frontend/src/application/threePresentation/**` contains no imports from Vue, Pinia, `OrbitControls`, `CSS2DRenderer`, `CSS2DObject`, `WebGLRenderer`, or `Scene` adapter classes. Selector files remain concern-split (`ProjectionPlane3DSelector`, `PlanarElement3DSelector`, `ReconstructedElement3DSelector`, `Guide3DSelector`, `Hinge3DSelector`/axis equivalent) rather than one god selector.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:210:  - new `application/threePresentation` selector tests,
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:212:  - `frontend/tests/unit/components/ThreeView.shell.spec.ts` if added,
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:224:If known project-level blockers from Wave 007 persist (missing eslint, `vue-tsc`/Node issue, malformed e2e specs), classify them with exact log output; do not skip the commands.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:228:- ThreeView shell: passes display options, injected `World`, and selected IDs to the runtime/controller, and contains no geometry, selected-domain-lookup, scene setup, label construction, or `scene.children` clearing logic.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:238:- **Risk: larger implementation than direct extraction.** Mitigation: keep selectors concern-split but narrowly scoped to current 3D view; no app-shell/persistence/tool changes.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:240:- **Risk: raw domain traversal simply moves from component to one giant selector.** Mitigation: split selectors by concern as a required design constraint and add architecture scans/tests for adapter/domain import direction and selector concern boundaries.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:243:- **Risk: e2e/live smoke cannot create required 3D state due existing e2e issues.** Mitigation: combine focused selector/adapter tests with live DOM/scene smoke and exact classification of external blockers.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:249:## Round 01 correction addendum — resolved blockers for the recommended path
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:253:### Explicit shell boundary and selected-ID data flow
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:255:`ThreeView.vue` is only a lifecycle/composition shell. It may read `viewStore`, `selectionStore`, and the injected `World` to assemble shell inputs, but it must pass selected IDs and display state into the application boundary as an explicit `threePresentation` input, for example `ThreePresentationInput { world, displayOptions, selectedIds }`. The component must not perform direct selected-element domain lookup, guide/perpendicular-plane derivation, projection-plane matrix interpretation, domain-to-view coordinate conversion, or raw Three.js object construction.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:259:### Concern-split selectors/read models are required, not optional
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:261:The top-level `ThreePresentationSelector` is only an orchestrator over separate selectors/read models. The implementation must keep these concerns split under `frontend/src/application/threePresentation/`:
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:268:- Axis/label selection may be a dedicated `Axis3DSelector`/`Label3DSelector` or a small submodule of the projection-plane selector, but it must not collapse guide, hinge, reconstructed-element, and planar-element traversal into one god file.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:270:One controller/runtime may compose these read models into a single `ThreePresentationModel`, but adapters must consume DTOs only and no selector file may become a renamed `ThreeView.vue`/`Element2DRenderer3D` traversal dump.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:285:- shell-boundary static scan for `ThreeView.vue` forbidding low-level Three.js construction, `scene.children` clearing, CSS2D object creation, projection-plane mesh helpers, guide/hinge geometry derivation, direct domain collection traversal, `realize2D(world)`, and `realize3D(world)`;
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:287:- selector tests for projection planes/meshes/grids/labels, planar 2D-on-3D elements, reconstructed 3D elements, selected-guide perpendicular-plane/intersection DTOs, hinge lines, axes, and domain-to-view conversion metadata;
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:289:- full mandatory cadence with stable logs: root lint, frontend lint, focused Vitest, full root Vitest, full frontend Vitest, root build, frontend build, Playwright/e2e or exact pre-existing blocker classification, live preview refresh/probe;
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:290:- live/e2e 3D smoke confirming `canvas.three-canvas` mounts, scene setup is delegated to runtime/host, display toggles refresh representative render groups, selected-guide flow produces guide DTO/object behavior when geometry exists, and preview reachability is recorded.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:292:These requirements preserve the Wave 008 scope and avoid Wave 009 app-shell drift: no `App.vue`, backend, persistence, command/tool, or 2D canvas restructuring is included except tiny shared pure policies/utilities if necessary. They also preserve no-backcompat/aggressive-deletion priorities by requiring deletion of `Element2DRenderer3D`, inline `ThreeView.vue` geometry/mesh helpers, raw-`World` scene adapters, compatibility shims, obsolete tests/fixtures, duplicated 2D/3D render special cases, and debug logging.
