architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/manager-scope-test-section.stdout:14:- A debug e2e spec points at `http://localhost:5180` (`frontend/tests/e2e/debug.spec.ts:3-11`), while the main e2e specs use `http://localhost:5173` or `/` (`frontend/tests/e2e/hhl-intersection.spec.ts:17`, `frontend/tests/e2e/parametric-update.spec.ts:18`); Wave 008 validation should record the live-preview URL/probe explicitly instead of assuming debug-spec coverage of the 3D view.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/manager-scope-test-section.stdout:15:- No current unit-test file path in `frontend/tests/` matches `ThreeView` or `Element2DRenderer3D` by filename, so Wave 008 implementation should add focused tests for the new 3D presentation selector DTOs and adapter object creation rather than relying on existing domain/e2e coverage.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-01-review.md:15:**BLOCKING ISSUES**
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-01-review.md:17:The wave premise is correct and both proposals are directionally strong. **Proposal Restructure is the better fit** for Wave 008 because it cleanly applies the Wave 007 selector/read-model pattern to the 3D path and explicitly deletes the `Element2DRenderer3D` raw-`World` renderer smell. However, neither proposal is ready for decision unchanged: both need in-place corrections so the review artifact enforces the 3D shell boundary and avoids leaving selection/store coupling and guide-plane math half-inside `ThreeView.vue`.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-01-review.md:21:- Wave 008 explicitly requires `ThreeView.vue` to become a lifecycle/composition shell and to isolate scene adapters/selectors (`architecture-audit/wave-plan.md:429`).
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-01-review.md:31:   It would materially shrink `ThreeView.vue`, but it leaves too much ambiguity about whether selection-store reads and guide/perpendicular-plane domain math remain in the shell or leak into adapters.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-01-review.md:40:   It stays near current behavior and does not pull in Wave 009 shell work.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-01-review.md:46:   Strong static scans and focused-test intent, but it should explicitly require a shell-boundary scan proving `ThreeView.vue` no longer imports domain projection/guide types or `Element2DRenderer3D` replacements that still take `World`.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-01-review.md:51:   Best match to Wave 008: `ThreeView.vue` becomes a shell, application selectors own read-model construction, and scene adapters consume DTOs only.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-01-review.md:54:   It directly prevents the `Element2DRenderer3D` architecture from reappearing under a new filename and aligns with the Wave 007 selector/controller pattern without reopening Wave 007.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-01-review.md:63:   The main risk is size/coordination across selectors and adapters, but the dependency rules are clearer and safer than Direct.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-01-review.md:66:   Good architecture scans, focused tests, mandatory cadence, and live preview checks. It still needs explicit coverage that the selected-guide/perpendicular-plane behavior and CSS2D label lifecycle are preserved after extraction.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-01-review.md:70:### 1) Make the shell boundary explicit for selection and guide behavior
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-01-review.md:74:Why this matters: the current guide/perpendicular-plane path is one of the densest cross-layer leaks in the component (`frontend/src/components/panels/ThreeView.vue:611`). If not called out explicitly, a “shell” implementation could still keep the hardest domain-to-view math in the component and only move easier helpers.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-01-review.md:76:### 2) Require concern-split selectors, not one replacement god-module
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-01-review.md:78:Both proposals should be edited to make the split non-optional: projection planes, planar 2D-on-3D elements, reconstructed 3D elements, guides, and hinges must be separate selector concerns under `application/threePresentation/`, even if orchestrated by one top-level controller. Do not allow one large `ThreePresentationSelector` file to absorb all current `ThreeView.vue` and `Element2DRenderer3D` traversal.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-01-review.md:92:It better matches the Wave 008 target outcome, better reuses Wave 007’s selector/read-model discipline, and is more honest about deleting `Element2DRenderer3D` instead of merely relocating it. Proposal Direct can remain as fallback, but only if it is tightened to the same non-negotiable boundary rules.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-01-review.md:96:- Good: neither proposal pulls in Wave 009 `App.vue` shell extraction.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-01-review.md:99:- Required during implementation: do not reopen Wave 007 2D selector/renderer extraction except for small shared style/visibility/read-model policies.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-02-review.md:14:**NO BLOCKING ISSUES**
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-02-review.md:16:The round-01 blockers were substantively resolved in both corrected proposals. **Proposal Restructure remains the recommended path** and is now implementation-ready for decision. Proposal Direct is also materially improved, but it remains the weaker fallback because it still frames the work as a smaller extraction, while Proposal Restructure more clearly enforces the application read-model boundary that Wave 008 needs.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-02-review.md:18:## Round-01 blocker disposition
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-02-review.md:20:### Blocker 1 — explicit shell boundary for selection and guide behavior
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-02-review.md:27:- `proposal-direct.md` now contains `Non-negotiable shell and selector boundaries` plus the addendum section `Shell boundary for selection, guide behavior, and scene construction`, stating that `ThreeView.vue` may read UI state but must not perform selected-element domain lookup, guide/perpendicular-plane derivation, realization traversal, or raw Three.js object construction.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-02-review.md:28:- `proposal-restructure.md` now contains the same constraint in stronger form under `Rules` and `Explicit shell boundary and selected-ID data flow`, requiring `ThreeView.vue` to pass `{ world, displayOptions, selectedIds }` into the runtime/presentation boundary and forbidding guide/perpendicular-plane derivation in the shell.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-02-review.md:32:### Blocker 2 — require concern-split selectors, not one replacement god-module
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-02-review.md:38:- `corrections-round-01-note.md` records explicit separate selector/read-model responsibilities for projection planes, planar elements, reconstructed elements, guides, hinges, and axis/label geometry.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-02-review.md:39:- `proposal-direct.md` now says `ThreePresentationSelector.ts` is a thin orchestrator only and names separate focused selectors: `ProjectionPlane3DSelector`, `PlanarElement3DSelector`, `ReconstructedElement3DSelector`, `Guide3DSelector`, and `HingeAxis3DSelector`.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-02-review.md:40:- `proposal-restructure.md` now makes the split non-optional under `Concern-split selectors/read models are required, not optional`, naming `ProjectionPlane3DSelector`, `PlanarElement3DSelector`, `ReconstructedElement3DSelector`, `Guide3DSelector`, `Hinge3DSelector`, and dedicated axis/label concern handling.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-02-review.md:42:This resolves the round-01 concern that Wave 008 could devolve into a rename wave that moves `ThreeView.vue` + `Element2DRenderer3D` complexity into one new god selector.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-02-review.md:58:The round-01 scoring still largely stands. Only blocker disposition changed.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-02-review.md:63:   The explicit shell boundary and required selector split now make it materially closer to the wave target.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-02-review.md:73:   The tightened gates now explicitly cover shell-boundary scans, adapter/registry tests, CSS2D cleanup, grouped replacement, and live/e2e smoke.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-02-review.md:78:   Best match for turning `ThreeView.vue` into a shell and moving domain traversal into application selectors.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-02-review.md:86:   The main risk is implementation coordination across runtime/selectors/adapters, but the boundaries are now clear enough to make that risk acceptable.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-02-review.md:88:   Validation now explicitly covers shell extraction, selector/adapter boundaries, disposal, CSS2D lifecycle, mandatory command cadence, and live 3D smoke.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-02-review.md:92:- **Selected-guide shell boundary:** satisfied in both proposals; strongest in Proposal Restructure.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-02-review.md:93:- **Concern-split selectors:** satisfied in both proposals; explicitly mandatory.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-02-review.md:96:- **Wave 009 exclusion:** satisfied; both proposals explicitly keep `App.vue`/app-shell work out of scope.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-02-review.md:100:These are not blockers, but the decision artifact should disclose them honestly:
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-02-review.md:102:- The restructure path is larger than the direct extraction path and will need disciplined implementation to avoid boundary drift between selectors, runtime, and adapters.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-02-review.md:103:- The proposals depend on focused architecture scans to enforce import-direction and shell-boundary rules; implementation review should verify those scans are actually added to validation logs.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/reviews/round-02-review.md:110:It now meets the review requirements, resolves all round-01 blockers, best matches the Wave 008 target outcome, and preserves correct scope: isolate a 3D presentation/read-model boundary, delete `Element2DRenderer3D`, make `ThreeView.vue` a lifecycle shell, validate grouped replacement/CSS2D cleanup, reuse the Wave 007 selector pattern where relevant, and avoid Wave 009 app-shell drift.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/validation/t1-corrections-diff-check.stdout:14:-## Blocker 1 — Make shell boundary explicit for selection and guide behavior
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/validation/t1-corrections-diff-check.stdout:15:+Reviewer verdict: **BLOCKING ISSUES**. Proposal Restructure remains the recommended path, but both proposals needed in-place tightening before round-02 review.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/validation/t1-corrections-diff-check.stdout:17:-Reviewer blocker: both proposals needed to state that `ThreeView.vue` may read UI state but must not keep guide/perpendicular-plane geometry derivation, direct selected-element domain lookup, or raw Three.js object construction. Selected IDs must flow into `threePresentation` input and come back as DTOs.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/validation/t1-corrections-diff-check.stdout:21:+### Blocker 1 — Make the shell boundary explicit for selection and guide behavior
