architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/validation/t1-corrections-diff-check.stdout:25:-- `proposals/proposal-direct.md` validation now requires a shell-boundary scan proving `ThreeView.vue` only passes display options, injected `World`, and selected IDs into the runtime/controller.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/validation/t1-corrections-diff-check.stdout:26:-- `proposals/proposal-restructure.md` now states the Vue shell may read `viewStore`/`selectionStore` only for UI state and must pass selected IDs into `runtime.refresh({ world, displayOptions, selectedIds })`; guide/perpendicular-plane DTOs must be produced by `threePresentation`.
